{"id": "D01", "question": "What do we need to do before engaging a third-party AI vendor?", "sector": "bank", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_cps230_2026:p52", "apra_cps230_2026:p55", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s006", "naic_ai6_foundations:s010"], "expected_tiers": ["binding", "expectation", "voluntary"], "reference_answer": "Mandatory: an AI vendor is a service provider; before entering a material arrangement CPS 230 para 52 requires due diligence and an assessment of financial and non-financial risks. Regulator expects: APRA's AI letter expects mapping of the AI supply chain, transparency/auditability in contracts and concentration-risk management. Recommended: AI6 suggests asking suppliers for proof of testing.", "retrieved_ids": ["naic_ai6_foundations:s009", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s021.3", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s033", "naic_ai6_foundations:s006", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s021.2", "naic_ai6_foundations:s002", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s016.1", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s006", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.3"], "retrieved_tiers": ["voluntary", "expectation", "expectation", "voluntary", "expectation", "voluntary", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.0, "rr": 0.125, "binding_coverage": 0.0, "binding_gold_hit": 0.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 4.714180427999963}
{"id": "D02", "question": "What must the contract with a provider of an AI model include if we rely on it for a critical operation?", "sector": "insurer", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_cps230_2026:p53", "apra_cps230_2026:p54", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s006"], "expected_tiers": ["binding", "expectation"], "reference_answer": "Mandatory: CPS 230 paras 53-54 require a formal legally binding agreement specifying services and service levels, rights and responsibilities (incl. data ownership, audit access), and provisions allowing APRA access. Regulator expects: contractual arrangements giving transparency, auditability and assurance over AI services (APRA AI letter).", "retrieved_ids": ["apra_ai_letter_2026:s006", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s033", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.3", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.4", "naic_ai6_foundations:s009", "naic_ai6_foundations:s002", "naic_ai6_foundations:s006", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s016.1"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "voluntary", "voluntary", "voluntary", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.3333333333333333, "rr": 1.0, "binding_coverage": 0.0, "binding_gold_hit": 0.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.025329059999990022}
{"id": "D03", "question": "Do we have to tell APRA when we start using an AI provider for a critical operation?", "sector": "bank", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_cps230_2026:p60"], "expected_tiers": ["binding"], "reference_answer": "Mandatory: CPS 230 para 60(a) - notify APRA as soon as possible and not more than 20 business days after entering into or materially changing an agreement for a service relied on for a critical operation; para 60(b) prior notice for material offshoring.", "retrieved_ids": ["apra_cpg230_2026:p18", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s002.1", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s007", "apra_cpg230_2026:p15", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s002.2", "apra_cpg230_2026:p2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.2", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s006", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s002.3"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.0, "rr": 0.0, "binding_coverage": 0.0, "binding_gold_hit": 0.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.024515079000025253}
{"id": "D04", "question": "Who in the organisation is accountable for risks from AI systems?", "sector": "bank", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_cps230_2026:p19", "apra_cps230_2026:p21", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s005", "naic_ai6_foundations:s006"], "expected_tiers": ["binding", "expectation", "voluntary"], "reference_answer": "Mandatory: the Board is ultimately accountable for oversight of operational risk management (CPS 230 paras 19-21). Regulator expects: ownership and accountability across the AI lifecycle (APRA AI letter). Recommended: AI6 practice 1 - assign a senior AI governance owner and an accountable person per AI system.", "retrieved_ids": ["naic_ai6_foundations:s006", "naic_ai6_foundations:s011", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.4", "naic_ai6_foundations:s003", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s002.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s028", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s007", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s005", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s002.1"], "retrieved_tiers": ["voluntary", "voluntary", "expectation", "voluntary", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.25, "rr": 1.0, "binding_coverage": 0.0, "binding_gold_hit": 0.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.02358550499991452}
{"id": "D05", "question": "What are our obligations to secure an AI system that processes customer data?", "sector": "super", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_cps234:p15", "apra_cps234:p21", "apra_cps230_2026:p24", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s004.1", "naic_ai6_foundations:s010"], "expected_tiers": ["binding", "expectation", "voluntary"], "reference_answer": "Mandatory: an AI system is an information asset - CPS 234 requires an information security capability and controls commensurate with threats (paras 15, 21); CPS 230 para 24 requires sound IT capability and compliance with CPS 234. Regulator expects: uplift of security practices for AI threats (APRA AI letter). Recommended: extend data governance and cyber practices to AI (AI6 5.4).", "retrieved_ids": ["oaic_ai_products_2025:s002.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s028", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s016.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s015.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s016.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s034.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s021.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s021.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s031.1"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.0, "rr": 0.0, "binding_coverage": 0.0, "binding_gold_hit": 0.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.023835344000076475}
{"id": "D06", "question": "If our AI vendor manages our information assets, what must we check about their security?", "sector": "bank", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_cps234:p16", "apra_cps234:p22", "apra_cps234:p28"], "expected_tiers": ["binding"], "reference_answer": "Mandatory: CPS 234 requires assessing the third party's information security capability (para 16), evaluating the design of its controls (para 22) and, where relying on its control testing, assessing that testing (para 28).", "retrieved_ids": ["oaic_ai_products_2025:s034.4", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s015.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s034.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s034.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s032.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s016.2", "naic_ai6_foundations:s010", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s032.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s002.1"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "voluntary", "expectation", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.0, "rr": 0.0, "binding_coverage": 0.0, "binding_gold_hit": 0.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.024082281999994848}
{"id": "D07", "question": "We had a serious outage of our AI-driven claims triage system. What are our notification obligations?", "sector": "insurer", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_cps230_2026:p41", "apra_cps230_2026:p32", "apra_cps230_2026:p35"], "expected_tiers": ["binding"], "reference_answer": "Mandatory: claims processing is a minimum critical operation for insurers (CPS 230 para 35); a disruption outside tolerance must be notified to APRA within 24 hours (para 41); an operational risk incident likely to have material impact within 72 hours (para 32).", "retrieved_ids": ["apra_cpg230_2026:s004", "apra_cps234:p35", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s028", "apra_cps230_2026:p41", "apra_cps230_2026:p32", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s031.2", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s008", "apra_cps220:p53", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s034.4"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "binding", "expectation", "binding", "binding", "expectation", "expectation", "binding", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.6666666666666666, "rr": 0.25, "binding_coverage": 1.0, "binding_gold_hit": 1.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.02313528399997722}
{"id": "D08", "question": "We plan to use an AI model to approve loans. What controls and monitoring are required?", "sector": "bank", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_cps230_2026:p28", "apra_cps230_2026:p29", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s007", "naic_ai6_foundations:s011"], "expected_tiers": ["binding", "expectation", "voluntary"], "reference_answer": "Mandatory: design, implement and embed internal controls and regularly monitor, review and test them (CPS 230 paras 28-29). Regulator expects: continuous validation/monitoring for drift and bias and integrated assurance (APRA AI letter). Recommended: meaningful human oversight and override points (AI6 practice 6).", "retrieved_ids": ["naic_ai6_foundations:s011", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.4", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s007", "naic_ai6_foundations:s010", "naic_ai6_foundations:s006", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s034.4", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s021.3", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.3", "naic_ai6_foundations:s001.2"], "retrieved_tiers": ["voluntary", "expectation", "expectation", "voluntary", "voluntary", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "voluntary"], "recall_at_5": 0.5, "rr": 1.0, "binding_coverage": 0.0, "binding_gold_hit": 0.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.022880706000023565}
{"id": "D09", "question": "Does our risk appetite statement need to cover AI?", "sector": "bank", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_cps220:p27", "apra_cps220:p28", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s002.2"], "expected_tiers": ["binding", "expectation"], "reference_answer": "Mandatory: CPS 220 requires a Board-approved risk appetite statement addressing material risks with tolerances (paras 27-28) - it does not mention AI but applies where AI is a material risk. Regulator expects: an AI strategy consistent with risk appetite and tolerance settings (APRA AI letter).", "retrieved_ids": ["apra_cps220:p27", "apra_cps220:p28", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s002.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s014.1", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s002.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s015.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s028", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s008"], "retrieved_tiers": ["binding", "binding", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.6666666666666666, "rr": 1.0, "binding_coverage": 1.0, "binding_gold_hit": 1.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.022118131000070207}
{"id": "D10", "question": "Do we need an inventory of our AI systems?", "sector": "super", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_ai_letter_2026:s005", "naic_ai6_foundations:s009", "apra_cps234:p20"], "expected_tiers": ["binding", "expectation", "voluntary"], "reference_answer": "Regulator expects: an inventory of AI tooling and AI use cases (APRA AI letter). Recommended: create and maintain an AI register (AI6 4.1). Mandatory (tech-neutral): CPS 234 para 20 requires classifying information assets, which includes AI systems.", "retrieved_ids": ["oaic_ai_products_2025:s021.3", "naic_ai6_foundations:s002", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s034.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s034.4", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s034.2", "naic_ai6_foundations:s009", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s028", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s014.1"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "voluntary", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "voluntary", "expectation", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.0, "rr": 0.14285714285714285, "binding_coverage": 0.0, "binding_gold_hit": 0.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.020511545000090337}
{"id": "D11", "question": "How should internal audit cover our use of AI?", "sector": "insurer", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_cps230_2026:p61", "apra_cps234:p32", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s007"], "expected_tiers": ["binding", "expectation"], "reference_answer": "Mandatory: internal audit must review proposed material outsourcing of critical operations (CPS 230 para 61) and review information security controls (CPS 234 para 32). Regulator expects: second line and internal audit to have technical capability and tooling to assess AI systems (APRA AI letter).", "retrieved_ids": ["oaic_ai_products_2025:s032.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s032.2", "naic_ai6_foundations:s005", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.4", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s033", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s007", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s034.4", "naic_ai6_foundations:s009", "naic_ai6_foundations:s011"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "expectation", "voluntary", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "voluntary", "voluntary"], "recall_at_5": 0.0, "rr": 0.16666666666666666, "binding_coverage": 0.0, "binding_gold_hit": 0.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.020868762000077368}
{"id": "D12", "question": "What should we do about concentration risk from relying on a single AI provider?", "sector": "bank", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_ai_letter_2026:s006", "apra_cpg230_2026:p54", "apra_cps230_2026:p52"], "expected_tiers": ["binding", "expectation"], "reference_answer": "Regulator expects: active management of concentration risk incl. credible substitution/exit for critical AI providers (APRA AI letter); consider concentration risk when selecting providers (CPG 230 para 54). Mandatory: assess risks incl. concentration of the service provider before entering a material arrangement (CPS 230 para 52(b)).", "retrieved_ids": ["apra_ai_letter_2026:s006", "naic_ai6_foundations:s008", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s014.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s014.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s013", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s002.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s006.1", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s007", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s008"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "voluntary", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.3333333333333333, "rr": 1.0, "binding_coverage": 0.0, "binding_gold_hit": 0.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.02258588199993028}
{"id": "D13", "question": "Must we keep a business continuity plan for critical operations that depend on AI?", "sector": "super", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["apra_cps230_2026:p33", "apra_cps230_2026:p39", "apra_cps230_2026:p42"], "expected_tiers": ["binding"], "reference_answer": "Mandatory: maintain a register of critical operations and a credible BCP (CPS 230 para 33) with prescribed contents (para 39) and a systematic testing program (para 42) - applies whether or not the operation uses AI.", "retrieved_ids": ["oaic_ai_products_2025:s033", "apra_cps230_2026:p33", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s006", "apra_cps230_2026:p39", "naic_ai6_foundations:s006", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s030.2", "naic_ai6_foundations:s011", "naic_ai6_foundations:s002", "naic_ai6_foundations:s001.2"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "binding", "expectation", "binding", "voluntary", "expectation", "voluntary", "voluntary", "voluntary"], "recall_at_5": 0.6666666666666666, "rr": 0.5, "binding_coverage": 1.0, "binding_gold_hit": 1.0, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.022507306000079552}
{"id": "D14", "question": "Our staff are using public generative AI chatbots. What rules apply?", "sector": "any_business", "type": "split", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["oaic_ai_products_2025:s021.3", "apra_ai_letter_2026:s004.1", "naic_ai6_foundations:s006"], "expected_tiers": ["expectation", "voluntary"], "reference_answer": "Regulator expects: as best practice do not enter personal (especially sensitive) information into publicly available AI tools (OAIC); APRA is concerned about enterprise AI tools used outside approved control frameworks (APRA AI letter). Recommended: an AI policy advising staff on AI risks (AI6 1.2).", "retrieved_ids": ["oaic_ai_products_2025:s011.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s035.4", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s022", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s021.3", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s007.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s029", "naic_ai6_foundations:s009", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s003.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s006.1"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "voluntary", "expectation", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.3333333333333333, "rr": 0.25, "binding_coverage": null, "binding_gold_hit": null, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.021320564000006925}
{"id": "D15", "question": "When does the APP 1.7-1.9 automated decision-making transparency obligation commence?", "sector": "any_business", "type": "factual", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["oaic_app1_adm_2026:s001"], "expected_tiers": ["expectation"], "reference_answer": "From 10 December 2026 (not yet in force as of November 2026).", "retrieved_ids": ["oaic_app1_adm_2026:s001", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s002", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s006", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s031.2", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s031.1", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s007.10", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s007.7", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s004.1", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s003"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 1.0, "rr": 1.0, "binding_coverage": null, "binding_gold_hit": null, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.02267374899997776}
{"id": "D16", "question": "When is an organisation in scope of the APP 1.7-1.9 transparency obligation?", "sector": "any_business", "type": "factual", "answerable": true, "gold_chunk_ids": ["oaic_app1_adm_2026:s002", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s004.1"], "expected_tiers": ["expectation"], "reference_answer": "Where it has arranged for a computer program to make, or do a thing substantially and directly related to making, a decision that could reasonably be expected to significantly affect an individual's rights or interests, using their personal information.", "retrieved_ids": ["oaic_app1_adm_2026:s002", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s001", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s006", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s031.1", "oaic_ai_products_2025:s031.2", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s007.10", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s005", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s007.7", "oaic_app1_adm_2026:s007.1"], "retrieved_tiers": ["expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation", "expectation"], "recall_at_5": 0.5, "rr": 1.0, "binding_coverage": null, "binding_gold_hit": null, "retrieval_latency_s": 0.02263213999992786}
